## 3. Modular ownership boundaries

The branch preserves the event-surface split:

```text
runtime/bus/actionEvent.mjs
  validation and normalization of action-event envelopes only

runtime/bus/actionEventHistory.mjs
  bounded in-memory retention, sequence assignment, duplicate retained eventId rejection, and read/query only

runtime/bus/actionEventSubscriptionRegistry.mjs
  live same-process listener registration, actionId/runId/type filtering, publication, and unsubscribe behavior only

runtime/bus/actionEventReplay.mjs
  optional retained in-memory replay plus live-join buffering/dedupe only

runtime.mjs
  composition root / dependency injection / public API export only
```

No broad event manager was introduced.

`actionEventReplay.mjs` does not import or own:

```text
runtime.mjs
workerBridge.mjs
llama_worker/**
runtime/request/**
runtime/stream/**
runtime/lifecycle/**
runtime/backends/**
runtime/router/**
runtime/services/**
executeAction internals
```

---

## 4. Replay behavior

When `options.replay !== true`, `subscribeActionEvents(...)` delegates to the existing live subscription registry and remains backward compatible.

When replay is enabled:

```text
1. subscription arguments and replay options are normalized/validated first;
2. a live subscription wrapper is registered before reading retained history;
3. matching live events are buffered until replay completes;
4. retained history is read with the normalized live filter plus replay cursor options;
5. retained events are delivered in existing history order;
6. buffered live events whose sequence is greater than the retained replay boundary are flushed;
7. future live events are delivered directly.
```

Boundary rule:

```text
No event should be missed between retained-history read and live registration.
An event already delivered by retained replay should not be delivered again from the join buffer.
```

Dedupe uses monotonic `sequence`, not eventId string comparison.

Listener errors during replay are isolated and do not abort the subscription surface, matching the live publication policy that listener failures must not affect other runtime behavior.

---

## 5. Public options

Replay options:

```js
{
    replay: true,
    afterSequence: 123,
    limit: 50
}
```

Validation:

```text
replay must be boolean when provided
afterSequence must be finite non-negative number when provided
limit must be positive integer when provided
unknown replay option keys reject before live registration
unknown live filter keys still reject through the subscription registry normalizer
```

Supported live filter keys remain:

```text
actionId
runId
type
```

This branch does not expand live subscriptions to support `capability`, timestamp range, or other history-only filters.

